### Q1. Which option, and why? (Plus missing option E and systemic scope from W)

* **Choice under current rules: Modified Option A (`REOPEN` to `held`)** (`B:39-41`)[cite: 1]. The owner's 2026-10-17 directive requires two things jointly: (1) *"Fable's stage is recorded as a HELD marker carrying its question (`[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` plus a `hold_question`) and is answered when the seat comes back"* (`B:9-11`), and (2) *"record a wall as a SEAT FAILURE, never as agreement"* (`B:11-12`)[cite: 1]. Meanwhile, `check_stage_panels.py` (`H:13-15, 39-41`) unconditionally raises `CLOSED-WHILE-HELD` if any stage in `STAGES = ("assess", "research", "review")` (`B:25`) has a non-empty `live_holds()` on a row with `row.get("state") == "closed"`[cite: 1, 2]. Options B and C (`B:42-45`) violate `B:10` by substituting `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` for `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` on the walled `research`/`review` stage (leaving `live_holds()` empty in `H:26` so the stage reads `ok 9/9` on stale answers, `B:31-32`)[cite: 1, 2]. Option D (`B:46`) leaves the walls counted as `is_answer() == True` (`T:17`), violating `B:11-12`[cite: 1, 2].
* **Reading of *"do not block a ruling or a commit on Fable"* and the missing Option E (`B:37, 50-51`):** Under Option A, neither the panel's **ruling** (by Astra + Grok + GLM 5.3, `B:9`) nor the code/ledger **commit** is blocked: the code fix and ruling commit normally while the ledger row's state is `held` (or `in work`, `B:32-33`, `H:16-18, 42-47`) awaiting Fable[cite: 1, 2]. However, if the owner intended *"do not block a ruling or a commit"* (`B:9`) to also mean *"do not block row closure (`state: closed`) when Astra + Grok + GLM 5.3 have approved closure"*, the brief's option list (`B:37-46`) lacks **Option E (`KEEP CLOSED, EXEMPT FABLE5 HOLDS IN H`)**: prefix `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` to the walled stage entries and extend `hold_question` (obeying `B:9-12`), keep the 9 rows `closed`, and amend `H:13-15, 39-41` so a `closed` row whose only `live` holds are `fable5` appends to `held` instead of `CLOSED-WHILE-HELD` `violations` (matching how `regress` holds already sit on `closed` rows, `B:20-21, 28`)[cite: 1, 2].
* **Closure objects under Option A (`B:40-41`):** Whether `check_stage_panels.py` (outside `H:1-47`) rejects a `closure` object on a non-`closed` row is **UNSETTLED** (settled by full `tools/pipeline/check_stage_panels.py`), though Astra's confirm on `ip30abortkill` explicitly ordered *"omit the closure object"* (`B:32-33`) so preserving the drafted closure text in the state note or hold note is the safe path[cite: 1, 2].
* **Angle 1 — Systemic scope (`W:1-36`) and structural check (`T:13-17`):**
  * **Scope:** Keep this fix scoped to the 16 post-2026-10-17 `fable5` entries in `C:6-55` plus `cxlaunchquotation` `[8]` (`2026-10-16`, `C:43`, an identical untokened `STALLED` `SEAT FAILURE` in the same review chain), and file the wider historical class (`497` entries across all `9` seats on `129` rows, `81` closed, from `2026-08` onward, `W:6-8`) as a separate row[cite: 1, 2]. `W:1, 3` warns that the keyword net is a correlate with known false positives (e.g., actual findings matching keywords in `W:19, 32, 33`), and many August/September entries (`W:11-28, 35`) were deliberate non-firings under earlier directives where `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` or stage exemption—not `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: ...]`—applies, or already-answered `"DEFANGED"` holds (`W:29-30`)[cite: 2].
  * **Structural check (not prose):** The root bug is `T:13-17`, where `is_answer(e)` defaults to `return True` (`T:17`) for every untokened entry[cite: 2]. To prevent any new untokened non-answer from being written: (1) add a structural check in `stage_tokens.py` / `check_stage_panels.py` that rejects (as a precommit violation) any entry where `is_answer(e)` is `True` (`T:13-17`) and `_note(e)`'s opening prefix matches the failure/non-firing markers (`NOT FIRED`, `SEAT FAILURE`, `walled`, `STALLED`, `not tried`, `HTTP 429`, `HTTP 529`, `usage limit`, `quota`, `403`, `DID NOT ANSWER`, `no answer`, `W:3-4`, `C:3`), or require an explicit positive answer token on all new answer entries so `T:17` never defaults untokened failure prose to `True`; and (2) make the panel-runner/ledger-writer automatically prepend `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: <seat>]` or `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` when recording a transport error/skip[cite: 1, 2].

### Q2. `cxlaunchquotation`, `dashokclass`, and `sgirekills` — held or discharged? (Angle 2: `T`'s `live_holds` vs `C`)

* **Angle 2 — Exact trace of `T:19-42` (`live_holds`) against `C:38-53` (`cxlaunchquotation` and `dashokclass`):**
  * `live_holds(entries)` (`T:25-41`) iterates over every entry `h` where `is_held(h)` is `True` (`T:26`), sets `hd = h.get("date") or ""` (`T:28`), and marks `seat` discharged (`done = True`) **only** if `any((e.get("seat") or "").lower() == seat and is_answer(e) and (e.get("date") or "") > hd for e in entries)` (`T:38-39`)[cite: 2].
  * **`cxlaunchquotation` (`C:38-45`):** The three census walls `[12]` (V3), `[26]` (V6), and `[30]` (V7) are all dated `2026-10-17` (`hd = "2026-10-17"`, `C:39-41`)[cite: 1]. Fable's other entries in `review` are dated `2026-10-16` (`[4]`, `[8]`, `C:42-43`) and `2026-10-17` (`[18]` V4, `[22]` V5, `C:44-45`)[cite: 1]. Because `T:39` requires strict date inequality `(e.get("date") or "") > hd` and `"2026-10-17" > "2026-10-17"` is `False`, **prefixing `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` leaves ALL THREE walls (`[12]`, `[26]`, `[30]`) LIVE, and neither the earlier `2026-10-16` answers (`[4]`, `[8]`) nor the later-index same-day `2026-10-17` answers (`[18]` V4, `[22]` V5) discharge ANY of them under `T:38-39`** (`C:39-45`, `T:28, 38-39`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * **`dashokclass` (`C:46-53`):** The census wall `[29]` (V7) is dated `2026-10-17` (`hd = "2026-10-17"`, `C:47`), while Fable's earlier answers are dated `2026-10-16` (`[2]`, `[6]`, `C:48-49`) and `2026-10-17` (`[15]` V3, `[17]` V4, `[21]` V5, `[25]` V6, `C:50-53`)[cite: 1]. None has `date > "2026-10-17"`, so **prefixing `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` leaves `[29]` LIVE and none of the earlier answers discharges it** (`C:47-53`, `T:28, 38-39`)[cite: 1, 2].
* **Substantive/repair-chain rule on `cxlaunchquotation`, `dashokclass`, and `sgirekills` (`B:52-55`):**
  * None of those three rows has its review (or research) stage discharged:
    1. On `cxlaunchquotation` (`C:42, 44-45`) and `dashokclass` (`C:48-53`), every earlier Fable answer was `SHIP WITH CHANGES` (finding breaches), never a zero-breach pass; when Fable walled on the closing pass V7 (`C:41, 47`), the repair-chain rule plus the 2026-10-17 directive (`B:9-12`) allowed the pass to proceed only by naming Fable's miss as `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` with a `hold_question`, not by treating earlier `SHIP WITH CHANGES` passes as discharging V7[cite: 1].
    2. On `cxlaunchquotation`, earlier intermediate failures `[8]` (v2, `2026-10-16`, `C:43`) and `[12]` (V3, `2026-10-17`, `C:39`) were superseded by Fable's actual V4 (`[18]`, `C:44`) and V5 (`[22]`, `C:45`) answers, and `[26]` (V6, `C:40`) was superseded by V7 (`[30]`, `C:41`)[cite: 1]. Either fix `T:38-39` to discharge same-day holds by later entry index (`e_idx > h_idx` when `e_date == hd`) and mark `[26]`/`[8]`/`[12]` `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` while marking `[30]` (V7) `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]`, or prefix `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` to `[30]` (the live V7 pass) and `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` to superseded earlier passes `[8]`, `[12]`, `[26]` (`C:39-41, 43`)[cite: 1, 2].
    3. On `sgirekills` (`C:13-18`), `research` `[45]` (`2026-10-17`, `C:14`) has zero other Fable entries in `research`, and `review` `[49]` (`2026-10-17`, `C:15`) and `[56]` (`2026-10-18`, `C:16`) only have prior-round answers from `2026-09-08` (`[28]`, `[38]`, `C:17-18`); both `research` and `review` are live holds[cite: 1].

### Q3. The conversion's form (`B:56-58`)

* **Prefix the token in place to the existing entry (one entry, provenance kept)** (`B:56`, `T:1-2, 13-17, 28, 38-39`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * `is_held(e)` tests `HELD in _note(e)` (`T:2`) and `is_answer(e)` returns `False` when `HELD in n or NOTSEAT in n` (`T:15-16`), so prefixing `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` directly to the existing entry simultaneously stops it from counting as an answer and registers the hold while preserving its original `date` (`hd` at `T:28`) and index[cite: 2].
  * Adding a new `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` entry today (`2026-10-18`) beside a re-tagged `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` entry would set `hd = "2026-10-18"` (`T:28`) on `2026-10-17` walls (`sgirekills` `[45]`, `[49]`, `cxlaunchquotation` `[12]`, `[26]`, `[30]`, `dashokclass` `[29]`, `C:14-15, 39-41, 47`), falsifying when the hold began and blocking any `2026-10-18` answer from discharging it under `(e.get("date") or "") > hd` (`T:39`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * Where multiple walled entries exist in the same `(row, phase)` because later passes ran (`wiringcliff` `[28]`/`[32]` already followed by `[41]`/`[48]` in `C:7-8, 11-12`; `sgirekills` `[49]` followed by `[56]` in `C:15-16`; `sgirandomcolour` `[28]` followed by `[32]` in `C:20-21`; `cxlaunchquotation` `[8]`/`[12]`/`[26]` followed by `[30]` in `C:39-41, 43`), either mark the superseded earlier pass attempts `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` and the latest pass `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]`, or fix `T:38-39` to compare `(e_date, e_idx) > (hd, h_idx)` so a single later answer discharges all prior holds in that stage regardless of whether they share a calendar date[cite: 1, 2].

### Q4. Is this an OWNER decision, and what is the single question? (`B:59-60`)

* Under the literal text of `B:9-12` and `H:13-15, 39-41` (and Astra's `ip30abortkill` confirm in `B:30-34`), reopening the nine rows to `held` (Option A) is already required by existing rules; however, deciding whether *"do not block a ruling or a commit on Fable"* (`B:9`) was meant to also permit row **closure** (`state: closed`) while a `fable5` stage hold remains live (Option E vs Option A) is an **owner policy decision**[cite: 1, 2].
* **Single question for the owner:**
  > *"When Astra + Grok + GLM 5.3 approve closing a row but Fable walled on `research` or `review` (`[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]`), must the row stay `state: held` until Fable answers (reopening the 9 rows closed since 2026-10-17), or should `check_stage_panels.py` section H allow `state: closed` with a live `fable5` stage hold just as it already allows `closed` with a `regress` hold?"* (`B:9-12, 20-21, 25-28, 39-41`, `H:13-15, 39-41`)[cite: 1, 2].

### Q5. Which of B's premises is wrong? (`B:61-62`)

1. **Census completeness (`B:14-18, 61` vs `C:2, 43`, `W:1-36`):** Incomplete. On `cxlaunchquotation` itself, entry `[8]` (`2026-10-16`, `C:43`) is an untokened `SEAT FAILURE` (`STALLED`) with `answer=True held=False` missed only because `C:2` filtered for `>= 2026-10-17`[cite: 1]. Across the ledger, `W:6-8` shows `497` untokened keyword-matched entries (`75` for `fable5`, including `59` before `2026-10-17`, `W:6, 10, 36`) across `129` rows (`81` closed)[cite: 2]. Whether additional post-2026-10-17 non-answers exist outside `C:2-3`'s 400-character keyword list is **UNSETTLED** without the working-tree ledger file[cite: 1].
2. **Later Fable answer discharging any of the nine closed rows (`B:61-62` vs `C:13-53`, `T:28, 38-39`):** None of the nine closed rows has a later Fable answer that discharges its stage[cite: 1, 2]. The only row among the nine where Fable answered after an included wall is `cxlaunchquotation`, where V4 (`[18]`, `2026-10-17`, `C:44`) and V5 (`[22]`, `2026-10-17`, `C:45`) came after V3 (`[12]`, `2026-10-17`, `C:39`), and those neither discharge V3 in `live_holds()` (because `"2026-10-17" > "2026-10-17"` is `False` at `T:39`) nor discharge the later walls on V6 (`[26]`, `C:40`) and V7 (`[30]`, `C:41`)[cite: 1, 2].
3. **`cxlaunchquotation` pass history (`B:52` vs `C:39-45`):** Fable did not answer V3-V6 and wall only on V7; it stalled on v2 (`[8]`, `C:43`) and V3 (`[12]`, `C:39`) and walled on V6 (`[26]`, `C:40`) as well as V7 (`[30]`, `C:41`)[cite: 1].
4. **`live_holds()` discharge rule description (`B:26, 57-58` vs `T:28, 38-39`):** `live_holds()` checks strictly later calendar `date` (`>`), not later entry order in the phase, so same-day recovery answers fail to discharge same-day holds (`T:39`)[cite: 1, 2].
5. **`wiringcliff` stage & hold status (`B:20-21, 25-28` vs `C:6-12`):** `wiringcliff` `[28]` is in `design` (not in `STAGES`, `B:25`, `C:7`), and `wiringcliff` already has `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` on later entries `[41]` (`design`, `C:11`) and `[48]` (`review`, `C:12`)[cite: 1].
6. **`ip30abortkill` state discrepancy (`B:32-33`):** `B:32-33` quotes Astra's confirm requiring `state: in work` and then states the row was committed `held`[cite: 1].

